{"metadata":{"title":"PostHogBatchEncoder","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostHogBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:15PostHogEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"PostHogBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder.swift#L77"},"modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PostHogBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of PostHog’s batch capture API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/batch\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/Failure"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogbatchencoder"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and PostHog’s limits:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"text":" with two members: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"api_key"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"project token, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name, then the members listed below"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked: ISO 8601 in UTC, with milliseconds (","type":"text"},{"code":"2026-11-23T14:03:27.512Z","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent, and every event is anonymous: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"text":" holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"text":", or one a store recovered after a relaunch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which keeps no context) is its own anonymous person, linked to nothing: PostHog rejects a whole","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch when one of its events has no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":". PostHog counts a person per ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so its unique users are sessions. The session is also sent as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"text":", which PostHog’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions and web analytics group events by (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property whose name starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which only a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write, or is ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names as settings (","type":"text"},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or the identity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$app_namespace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$app_build","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mobile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tablet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Desktop","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"TV","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Vision","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the form factor; no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a watch","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$locale","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$network_wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$network_cellular","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for PostHog to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. PostHog answers a batch it takes with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"200, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retries one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it rejects. A record sent again keeps its "},{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://PostHogEncoding/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"title":"BatchEncoder","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/Sensitive":{"abstract":[{"text":"A property value that a destination reads only through the record it arrived in, and not at all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once the record is redacted.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/events\/sensitive","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Sensitive","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogBatchEncoder/init(p